{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2008960","formula":"Na₃Fe₅Si₈H₂O₂₄","hill":"Fe5H2Na3O24Si8","elements":["H","O","Na","Si","Fe"],"composition":{"H":2.0,"O":24.0,"Fe":5.0,"Na":3.0,"Si":8.0},"names":{"en":"Arfvedsonite","ru":"Арфведсонит","uk":"Арфведсоніт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Arfvedsonite () or soda hornblende (partiellement obsolète) is a sodium amphibole mineral with composition: [Na][Na2][(Fe2+)4Fe3+][(OH)2|Si8O22]. It crystallizes in the monoclinic prismatic crystal system and typically occurs as greenish black to bluish grey fibrous to radiating or stellate prisms. It is a rather rare mineral occurring in nepheline syenite intrusions and agpaitic (peralkaline) pegmatites and granites as the Golden Horn batholith in Okanogan County, Washington (type locality for zektzerite).","ru":"Арфведсони́т — минерал класса силикатов. Относится к амфиболам, подсемейству щелочных амфиболов. Название минералу дано в честь шведского химика И. А. Арфведсона.","uk":"Арфведсоніт — мінерал, лужний амфібол ланцюжкової будови."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2008960","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arfvedsonite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D1%80%D1%84%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%B4%D1%81%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D1%80%D1%84%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%B4%D1%81%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arfvedsonit-167989.jpg","licen